1
00:00:25,926 --> 00:00:28,126
♪ ♪

2
00:00:36,470 --> 00:00:38,303
♪ ♪

3
00:00:49,383 --> 00:00:51,450
♪ ♪

4
00:01:20,448 --> 00:01:23,381
♪ ♪

5
00:02:25,379 --> 00:02:28,312
♪ ♪

6
00:02:32,786 --> 00:02:33,719
I'm sorry.

7
00:02:33,787 --> 00:02:34,920
Can you tell me again

8
00:02:34,988 --> 00:02:36,966
which coins you think
my husband would like?

9
00:02:36,990 --> 00:02:40,559
Well, judging from what
I know of his collection,

10
00:02:40,627 --> 00:02:42,594
it would either be this,

11
00:02:42,663 --> 00:02:45,964
which is $569, uh...

12
00:02:46,032 --> 00:02:51,002
or this, uh... which is $529.

13
00:02:51,070 --> 00:02:52,148
Oh.

14
00:02:52,172 --> 00:02:54,806
They're both beautiful.

15
00:02:56,242 --> 00:02:59,310
Damn, this is hard.

16
00:03:03,017 --> 00:03:05,851
Uh, Mrs. Hansfield, I have
to step out for a moment.

17
00:03:05,919 --> 00:03:07,396
Uh, when you've
made up your mind,

18
00:03:07,420 --> 00:03:09,854
Rob there will take care of you.

19
00:03:09,923 --> 00:03:10,856
Just take your time.

20
00:03:10,924 --> 00:03:12,204
Hmm...

21
00:03:14,962 --> 00:03:17,406
I can't stand this
another minute.

22
00:03:17,430 --> 00:03:19,843
Look after her while I
grab some lunch, will you?

23
00:03:19,867 --> 00:03:21,800
No problem.

24
00:03:27,841 --> 00:03:29,407
If you have any questions,

25
00:03:29,476 --> 00:03:30,409
just let me know.

26
00:03:30,477 --> 00:03:32,844
Sure.

27
00:04:27,100 --> 00:04:28,499
I can't decide.

28
00:04:31,705 --> 00:04:33,638
Do you sell gift certificates?

29
00:04:33,707 --> 00:04:36,507
Not ordinarily, no.

30
00:04:38,612 --> 00:04:41,512
Maybe I should just ask
him which coin he'd like.

31
00:04:42,816 --> 00:04:45,116
Ah, hell, maybe I'll
just buy him a tie.

32
00:04:45,185 --> 00:04:48,019
Tell Mr. Koskoff
thanks anyway, okay?

33
00:04:48,088 --> 00:04:49,521
Certainly.

34
00:05:09,809 --> 00:05:12,944
He took a coin out of the
safe and put it in his raincoat.

35
00:05:13,013 --> 00:05:14,212
You sure?

36
00:05:14,281 --> 00:05:15,561
Left-hand pocket.

37
00:05:15,615 --> 00:05:17,748
Follow him. I don't
want him to leave town

38
00:05:17,817 --> 00:05:20,418
till he gives back every
coin he's taken from me.

39
00:05:20,487 --> 00:05:21,786
You got it.

40
00:05:43,877 --> 00:05:45,810
That was fast.

41
00:05:45,879 --> 00:05:48,313
I lost my appetite.

42
00:05:48,382 --> 00:05:49,382
Get up.

43
00:05:59,159 --> 00:06:02,160
356 items in the inventory.

44
00:06:02,229 --> 00:06:04,563
There were 357 this morning.

45
00:06:04,631 --> 00:06:06,331
I made a sale.

46
00:06:06,399 --> 00:06:08,678
That, uh, Hansfield lady
who was just here. Oh...

47
00:06:08,702 --> 00:06:09,868
you liar.

48
00:06:12,272 --> 00:06:14,250
Here it is in your coat pocket.

49
00:06:14,274 --> 00:06:16,908
This coin is worth
more than $5,000.

50
00:06:16,977 --> 00:06:19,055
I know who Mr. Stryker is, Rob,

51
00:06:19,079 --> 00:06:20,490
the guy who keeps calling you.

52
00:06:20,514 --> 00:06:22,247
I listened last night.

53
00:06:22,315 --> 00:06:23,595
He's your bookie.

54
00:06:23,650 --> 00:06:25,361
Every time you owe
him some money,

55
00:06:25,385 --> 00:06:27,097
you steal a coin from the shop.

56
00:06:27,121 --> 00:06:28,264
Isn't that right?
Hey, Michael...

57
00:06:28,288 --> 00:06:29,799
I went over the
invoices last night.

58
00:06:29,823 --> 00:06:31,890
There's 11 coins, Rob.

59
00:06:31,958 --> 00:06:35,059
That's nearly
$40,000 worth missing.

60
00:06:35,129 --> 00:06:37,128
It wasn't me, I-I swear it.

61
00:06:37,197 --> 00:06:38,763
I want them back.

62
00:06:38,832 --> 00:06:41,032
I want every single coin

63
00:06:41,101 --> 00:06:43,446
you stole from me back.

64
00:06:43,470 --> 00:06:45,770
They're gone, all of 'em.

65
00:06:45,838 --> 00:06:47,505
Then I want the money!

66
00:06:47,574 --> 00:06:49,140
I want $40,000.

67
00:06:49,209 --> 00:06:50,587
Do you hear me? Forty...

68
00:06:50,611 --> 00:06:52,944
He can't breathe, Mr. K.

69
00:06:53,013 --> 00:06:54,223
I... I don't have it.

70
00:06:54,247 --> 00:06:57,415
Then get it, or I'm
going to call the police!

71
00:06:57,484 --> 00:06:59,784
You underst-understand?

72
00:07:01,155 --> 00:07:03,566
I'm not going to
be... ruined by a,

73
00:07:03,590 --> 00:07:05,468
by a piece of garbage like you.

74
00:07:05,492 --> 00:07:09,393
I want that money by Thursday.

75
00:07:09,462 --> 00:07:10,928
You understand me?

76
00:07:13,533 --> 00:07:16,834
♪ ♪

77
00:07:16,903 --> 00:07:19,337
<i>9:53... Rob Casey went</i>

78
00:07:19,406 --> 00:07:24,008
<i>to House Call Car Service, met
with the owner, Mitchell Sands.</i>

79
00:07:24,077 --> 00:07:26,010
<i>A bitter argument ensued.</i>

80
00:07:28,882 --> 00:07:30,815
♪ ♪

81
00:07:34,320 --> 00:07:38,856
<i>11:30... I followed Casey
to Vid-Proof off West Third.</i>

82
00:07:38,925 --> 00:07:40,892
<i>He met with Jeffrey Barr.</i>

83
00:07:40,961 --> 00:07:43,461
<i>A bitter argument ensued.</i>

84
00:07:54,540 --> 00:07:57,709
<i>12:22... Casey went directly</i>

85
00:07:57,777 --> 00:08:00,745
<i>to the suburban residence
of one Nancy Proctor.</i>

86
00:08:00,814 --> 00:08:02,347
<i>I checked her mailbox.</i>

87
00:08:02,416 --> 00:08:04,616
<i>Another argument ensued.</i>

88
00:08:04,684 --> 00:08:06,685
♪ ♪

89
00:08:26,473 --> 00:08:29,240
<i>The next day, it rained.</i>

90
00:08:31,745 --> 00:08:34,813
<i>2:24... I followed Rob Casey</i>

91
00:08:34,881 --> 00:08:37,615
<i>to the far west
end of Stryker Park.</i>

92
00:08:37,684 --> 00:08:39,984
<i>He stumbled around
in the underbush,</i>

93
00:08:40,053 --> 00:08:42,097
<i>finally found the tree
he was looking for,</i>

94
00:08:42,121 --> 00:08:45,089
<i>and dug up what
appears to be a strongbox.</i>

95
00:08:45,158 --> 00:08:47,069
<i>Then he set up a
camera on a tripod</i>

96
00:08:47,093 --> 00:08:50,394
<i>and took pictures of
himself with the box.</i>

97
00:09:08,748 --> 00:09:12,517
<i>4:42... The rain
finally stopped.</i>

98
00:09:12,586 --> 00:09:14,597
<i>Casey ran a red
light back into town.</i>

99
00:09:14,621 --> 00:09:16,265
<i>He went to a one-hour photo shop</i>

100
00:09:16,289 --> 00:09:19,090
<i>and spent 50 minutes inside.</i>

101
00:09:25,264 --> 00:09:28,833
<i>5:22... Casey went
directly to the post office,</i>

102
00:09:28,902 --> 00:09:31,903
<i>where he carried
some sort of case inside.</i>

103
00:10:00,533 --> 00:10:03,467
♪ ♪

104
00:10:08,475 --> 00:10:12,444
<i>5:45... Casey has
returned to his residence.</i>

105
00:10:12,512 --> 00:10:14,779
<i>He carried the case inside.</i>

106
00:10:27,227 --> 00:10:29,160
I'll be home soon, sweetheart.

107
00:10:29,229 --> 00:10:31,496
Oh, dinner's in
the refrigerator.

108
00:10:31,564 --> 00:10:32,797
Mm-hmm.

109
00:10:32,866 --> 00:10:35,800
And honey, give
Mrs. Waverly a break.

110
00:10:35,869 --> 00:10:38,136
Your ghost stories scare her.

111
00:10:39,373 --> 00:10:40,771
I love you, too, Davey.

112
00:10:40,840 --> 00:10:42,374
Bye-bye.

113
00:11:08,501 --> 00:11:10,301
Open up in there!

114
00:11:12,939 --> 00:11:14,873
What's going on?

115
00:11:27,287 --> 00:11:29,287
Anybody here?

116
00:11:31,424 --> 00:11:33,358
Hello?

117
00:11:57,484 --> 00:11:58,416
Hey.

118
00:11:58,485 --> 00:12:00,296
Mr. Koskoff. Yes?

119
00:12:00,320 --> 00:12:02,297
I'm Lieutenant Bob Brooks,
Atlanta Police Department.

120
00:12:02,321 --> 00:12:04,221
I'd like to ask you
some questions.

121
00:12:04,290 --> 00:12:05,301
What about?

122
00:12:05,325 --> 00:12:07,692
A man Rob Casey
was shot and killed

123
00:12:07,761 --> 00:12:08,926
yesterday evening.

124
00:12:08,995 --> 00:12:10,928
I understand he'd
worked for you.

125
00:12:10,997 --> 00:12:13,597
Yes. Yes, he did.

126
00:12:13,667 --> 00:12:16,901
Well, evidently, you and
he had a fight yesterday?

127
00:12:16,970 --> 00:12:19,737
He was stealing from me.

128
00:12:19,806 --> 00:12:23,574
Ah. Mr. Casey was
shot about 6:15.

129
00:12:23,643 --> 00:12:24,942
Where were you then?

130
00:12:26,012 --> 00:12:28,613
Y-You think I killed him.

131
00:12:28,682 --> 00:12:30,982
How could I get my
money back if I killed him?

132
00:12:31,051 --> 00:12:31,883
Where were you?

133
00:12:31,951 --> 00:12:34,886
Well, I...

134
00:12:34,954 --> 00:12:37,889
About 5:00 yesterday
afternoon I...

135
00:12:37,957 --> 00:12:39,891
I got a phone call from a man

136
00:12:39,959 --> 00:12:42,060
who said he had
some rare coins to sell,

137
00:12:42,128 --> 00:12:45,830
and he wanted me to
come to his home at 7:00.

138
00:12:45,899 --> 00:12:48,365
Can you give me the man's name?

139
00:12:48,435 --> 00:12:50,401
No, I can't.

140
00:12:50,469 --> 00:12:53,437
The address was out in Decatur,
and-and when I got out there

141
00:12:53,506 --> 00:12:56,441
all I found was an empty house
with a "for sale" sign in front.

142
00:12:59,112 --> 00:13:00,478
Excuse me.

143
00:13:06,486 --> 00:13:08,052
Mr. Koskoff,

144
00:13:08,121 --> 00:13:10,521
we found this gun in a
Dumpster down the block.

145
00:13:10,590 --> 00:13:11,790
Have you ever seen it before?

146
00:13:16,730 --> 00:13:20,264
<i>Ballistics says the gun was the
murder weapon and it's yours.</i>

147
00:13:20,333 --> 00:13:21,710
Look, the last time I saw it,

148
00:13:21,734 --> 00:13:23,746
it was on a shelf in my closet.

149
00:13:23,770 --> 00:13:25,536
How long ago was that?

150
00:13:25,605 --> 00:13:27,138
Oh, weeks, months.

151
00:13:27,206 --> 00:13:28,973
I don't know. Hmm.

152
00:13:29,041 --> 00:13:33,377
This victim... this,
uh, Rob Casey...

153
00:13:33,446 --> 00:13:36,314
Did he steal any
early American coins?

154
00:13:36,382 --> 00:13:37,393
Mmm, sometimes.

155
00:13:37,417 --> 00:13:40,151
Not the 1804 Silver Dollar.

156
00:13:40,220 --> 00:13:42,119
No. That's still in the case.

157
00:13:42,188 --> 00:13:43,188
I found

158
00:13:43,256 --> 00:13:45,356
an 1850 Liberty
Seated Silver Dollar

159
00:13:45,424 --> 00:13:46,424
over in Athens

160
00:13:46,459 --> 00:13:48,926
about a month ago
just in fair condition.

161
00:13:48,995 --> 00:13:51,863
When you were in, uh, Decatur

162
00:13:51,931 --> 00:13:53,943
looking at those coins,
did anybody see you?

163
00:13:53,967 --> 00:13:55,333
Well, of course not.

164
00:13:55,402 --> 00:13:56,500
I... Oh, yeah.

165
00:13:56,570 --> 00:13:59,504
I guess that was
the idea, wasn't it?

166
00:13:59,572 --> 00:14:01,305
Uh, the police say

167
00:14:01,374 --> 00:14:04,108
the woman who found
the body works for you.

168
00:14:04,177 --> 00:14:05,342
Uh, Hansfield.

169
00:14:05,411 --> 00:14:06,911
She's a private investigator.

170
00:14:06,980 --> 00:14:08,312
What was she doing at his house?

171
00:14:08,381 --> 00:14:09,513
She was following him.

172
00:14:09,582 --> 00:14:11,127
I wanted to make sure
he didn't leave town.

173
00:14:11,151 --> 00:14:15,864
Ben... whenever
you've been in my shop

174
00:14:15,888 --> 00:14:17,500
I've always been
honest with you.

175
00:14:17,524 --> 00:14:20,758
Well, now, I'm in your shop.

176
00:14:20,827 --> 00:14:22,960
What's gonna happen to me?

177
00:14:25,031 --> 00:14:26,431
I don't know.

178
00:14:27,867 --> 00:14:30,802
The murder weapon
belongs to you.

179
00:14:30,870 --> 00:14:33,805
A witness saw you
strangling the victim

180
00:14:33,873 --> 00:14:35,540
the day of the murder.

181
00:14:35,608 --> 00:14:37,040
You have no alibi.

182
00:14:37,110 --> 00:14:38,710
Take my case.

183
00:14:38,778 --> 00:14:39,844
Please.

184
00:14:41,948 --> 00:14:46,751
Well, Michael, my
fee is, uh, you know...

185
00:14:48,822 --> 00:14:51,155
The 1804 Silver Dollar is yours.

186
00:14:58,899 --> 00:15:01,599
I'll throw in the 1836
Gold Brick Proof.

187
00:15:04,704 --> 00:15:08,339
Give me the Liberty Seateds
through 1851, you got a deal.

188
00:15:10,010 --> 00:15:12,377
I'm not gonna sell 'em.
You can come see 'em.

189
00:15:20,553 --> 00:15:21,553
All right.

190
00:15:23,389 --> 00:15:25,167
Well... look at it
this way, Michael.

191
00:15:25,191 --> 00:15:28,760
You just got 100 grand
worth of legal services for $13.

192
00:15:51,851 --> 00:15:53,984
Come in.

193
00:15:58,024 --> 00:15:59,368
Hello. Hello.

194
00:15:59,392 --> 00:16:01,358
Uh, are you Linda Hansfield?

195
00:16:01,428 --> 00:16:02,571
Yes.

196
00:16:02,595 --> 00:16:04,506
Mr. Matlock, I've
been expecting you.

197
00:16:04,530 --> 00:16:05,730
Is that right?

198
00:16:05,798 --> 00:16:07,843
Yes, I heard you were
representing Mr. Koskoff.

199
00:16:07,867 --> 00:16:09,478
I thought you'd
want to talk to me.

200
00:16:09,502 --> 00:16:10,434
Oh.

201
00:16:10,503 --> 00:16:11,780
Would, would you
like some coffee?

202
00:16:11,804 --> 00:16:13,282
It's fresh. No thanks.

203
00:16:13,306 --> 00:16:14,671
Well, have a seat then.

204
00:16:14,740 --> 00:16:15,973
All right, thank you.

205
00:16:16,042 --> 00:16:19,477
Uh, Michael... Uh,
Mr. Koskoff... uh,

206
00:16:19,545 --> 00:16:21,646
said that you had
been following...

207
00:16:21,715 --> 00:16:23,880
Rob Casey.

208
00:16:23,950 --> 00:16:25,082
I was.

209
00:16:25,151 --> 00:16:27,017
Well, then, I guess you,

210
00:16:27,086 --> 00:16:29,353
as well as... Or maybe
better... than anyone,

211
00:16:29,422 --> 00:16:33,424
would know how he spent
the last two days of his life.

212
00:16:33,493 --> 00:16:38,396
I have a detailed account
of where he was and...

213
00:16:38,464 --> 00:16:41,098
who he was with right here.

214
00:16:42,201 --> 00:16:45,603
Uh, uh... could I look at it?

215
00:16:45,672 --> 00:16:47,605
I'll tell you what.

216
00:16:47,673 --> 00:16:49,273
I'll make you a copy.

217
00:16:49,342 --> 00:16:51,575
Oh, that'd be terrific.

218
00:16:53,679 --> 00:16:56,280
One condition.

219
00:16:56,349 --> 00:16:58,316
What's that?

220
00:17:01,420 --> 00:17:04,288
Mr. Matlock, as
you might expect,

221
00:17:04,357 --> 00:17:07,091
it's tough being a
woman in this business.

222
00:17:08,194 --> 00:17:09,194
Hmm...

223
00:17:11,297 --> 00:17:13,097
That's my boy.

224
00:17:14,567 --> 00:17:15,833
He's a fine-looking boy.

225
00:17:15,902 --> 00:17:17,367
Thanks.

226
00:17:17,436 --> 00:17:18,936
I'm proud of him.

227
00:17:19,005 --> 00:17:20,638
He's proud of me, too.

228
00:17:20,706 --> 00:17:22,451
Thinks his mom
has a really neat job.

229
00:17:22,475 --> 00:17:24,086
But usually,

230
00:17:24,110 --> 00:17:26,288
the only reason I get hired
is because somebody needs

231
00:17:26,312 --> 00:17:29,614
an investigator fast, and
I'm the only one available.

232
00:17:29,682 --> 00:17:30,915
You know what I need?

233
00:17:32,018 --> 00:17:34,418
Credibility.

234
00:17:34,487 --> 00:17:37,989
The kind I'd undoubtedly
get if, say, I were to spearhead

235
00:17:38,057 --> 00:17:41,959
a murder investigation for
a famous criminal attorney.

236
00:17:43,063 --> 00:17:46,630
I... I have an investigator.

237
00:17:46,699 --> 00:17:48,399
Oh.

238
00:17:49,968 --> 00:17:51,502
I have the notebook.

239
00:17:51,571 --> 00:17:53,237
What if it's worthless?

240
00:17:53,306 --> 00:17:55,239
What if it's not?

241
00:17:58,144 --> 00:17:59,777
Rob Casey talked to three people

242
00:17:59,846 --> 00:18:01,879
after he left
Mr. Koskoff's coin shop.

243
00:18:01,948 --> 00:18:04,115
Just three people.

244
00:18:04,183 --> 00:18:05,928
24 hours later, he was dead.

245
00:18:05,952 --> 00:18:08,819
Their names are right here.

246
00:18:10,924 --> 00:18:12,256
This is blackmail.

247
00:18:13,359 --> 00:18:15,125
I know.

248
00:18:22,668 --> 00:18:24,901
I must have missed
the killer by seconds.

249
00:18:24,970 --> 00:18:26,237
Hmm.

250
00:18:27,373 --> 00:18:28,950
You could've
gotten killed yourself.

251
00:18:28,974 --> 00:18:29,906
I had my gun.

252
00:18:29,975 --> 00:18:30,975
Huh.

253
00:18:40,653 --> 00:18:43,120
This the way whoever
it was came in?

254
00:18:43,189 --> 00:18:44,288
Had to be.

255
00:18:44,357 --> 00:18:46,524
I was watching the
front door the whole time.

256
00:18:46,593 --> 00:18:47,858
Back door was locked.

257
00:18:47,927 --> 00:18:48,927
Huh.

258
00:18:48,961 --> 00:18:49,961
What do you think?

259
00:18:50,029 --> 00:18:52,296
I think Rob Casey
knew his killer

260
00:18:52,365 --> 00:18:54,176
well enough to let
him in, don't you?

261
00:18:54,200 --> 00:18:55,399
Yeah.

262
00:18:57,470 --> 00:18:59,803
Hmm.

263
00:18:59,872 --> 00:19:01,472
That's nice.

264
00:19:02,741 --> 00:19:03,874
Hmm.

265
00:19:18,457 --> 00:19:19,523
What do you got?

266
00:19:20,627 --> 00:19:22,660
His camera.

267
00:19:22,729 --> 00:19:24,049
Shutter's set for
delayed release.

268
00:19:24,097 --> 00:19:25,395
Oh.

269
00:19:26,799 --> 00:19:29,466
Those are the people he
talked to the day before.

270
00:19:29,535 --> 00:19:30,646
And those are their addresses.

271
00:19:30,670 --> 00:19:33,203
Oh. Oh.

272
00:19:33,273 --> 00:19:37,174
Looks like he was gonna
send the same three pictures

273
00:19:37,243 --> 00:19:39,676
to all of them.

274
00:19:39,746 --> 00:19:41,857
This what he was wearing when
you followed him in the woods?

275
00:19:41,881 --> 00:19:43,280
Yeah.

276
00:19:43,349 --> 00:19:44,860
I followed him
to this photo lab.

277
00:19:44,884 --> 00:19:46,283
Yo!

278
00:19:46,352 --> 00:19:49,520
I would've got here sooner,
but I got stuck in traffic.

279
00:19:49,589 --> 00:19:51,533
There's a big pileup
over on Pine and Whitney.

280
00:19:51,557 --> 00:19:52,489
Hi.

281
00:19:52,559 --> 00:19:55,292
Hi. Do Pine and
Whitney intersect?

282
00:19:56,395 --> 00:19:58,262
Maybe it was Pike and Whitney.

283
00:19:58,331 --> 00:20:00,364
Uh, Tyler, this is
Linda Hansfield.

284
00:20:00,433 --> 00:20:02,143
Linda, Tyler Hudson.

285
00:20:02,167 --> 00:20:03,100
Hi, again.

286
00:20:03,169 --> 00:20:05,047
Hello. MATLOCK: Uh, well,

287
00:20:05,071 --> 00:20:07,116
keep looking, see if you
come up with anything else.

288
00:20:07,140 --> 00:20:08,918
I've got to go to
Mr. Koskoff's arraignment.

289
00:20:08,942 --> 00:20:13,210
Uh, fill in Tyler where we
are and get acquainted.

290
00:20:15,315 --> 00:20:17,447
So are you a
friend of Michelle's?

291
00:20:17,517 --> 00:20:19,216
No, I work here.

292
00:20:19,285 --> 00:20:21,518
Mm. What do you do?

293
00:20:21,588 --> 00:20:24,622
I'm a private investigator.

294
00:20:54,720 --> 00:20:56,654
♪ ♪

295
00:21:08,133 --> 00:21:09,433
May I help you?

296
00:21:09,501 --> 00:21:12,061
I'm looking for Mitchell Sands.

297
00:21:13,305 --> 00:21:14,305
Just a minute.

298
00:21:17,643 --> 00:21:20,177
Mitch.

299
00:21:24,884 --> 00:21:26,951
I'm Mitchell Sands.

300
00:21:29,055 --> 00:21:30,287
You own this place?

301
00:21:30,356 --> 00:21:31,288
Yes.

302
00:21:31,357 --> 00:21:33,623
It's amazing.

303
00:21:33,692 --> 00:21:36,860
I have never seen a repair shop
where you can eat off the floor.

304
00:21:38,430 --> 00:21:40,898
Well, like the sign says,
we make house calls.

305
00:21:40,967 --> 00:21:42,244
Something goes
wrong with your car,

306
00:21:42,268 --> 00:21:44,501
we go to your house and fix it.

307
00:21:44,570 --> 00:21:47,271
Uh, does your car
need repairing, Mr...

308
00:21:47,340 --> 00:21:48,405
Oh, Tyler Hudson.

309
00:21:49,575 --> 00:21:51,375
No, no, my car is fine.

310
00:21:51,444 --> 00:21:53,410
I wanted to ask you
about Rob Casey.

311
00:21:56,249 --> 00:21:58,260
You know, the gentleman
that you were seen talking to

312
00:21:58,284 --> 00:21:59,484
out front a couple days ago.

313
00:22:04,857 --> 00:22:07,090
I've never seen this man before.

314
00:22:07,160 --> 00:22:09,604
No, I've never
heard of Rob Casey.

315
00:22:09,628 --> 00:22:10,994
Hmm.

316
00:22:11,063 --> 00:22:12,529
Then why do you suppose

317
00:22:12,598 --> 00:22:14,765
he was going to send
you these pictures?

318
00:22:14,834 --> 00:22:16,145
I haven't the foggiest.

319
00:22:16,169 --> 00:22:19,737
Ms. Proctor...
Missus. I'm divorced.

320
00:22:19,805 --> 00:22:20,805
Yeah.

321
00:22:20,840 --> 00:22:23,374
Well, happens to
the best of us, uh...

322
00:22:23,443 --> 00:22:26,443
Mrs. Proctor, Rob Casey was here

323
00:22:26,512 --> 00:22:28,779
in this house talking to
you less than a week ago.

324
00:22:28,848 --> 00:22:30,981
I saw him with my own eyes.

325
00:22:32,051 --> 00:22:33,450
That's just not possible.

326
00:22:33,519 --> 00:22:34,784
Mom!

327
00:22:34,853 --> 00:22:37,413
Excuse me, I'll be right back.

328
00:22:41,927 --> 00:22:43,207
Adam, Adam...

329
00:23:02,615 --> 00:23:04,748
Her brother's
picking on her again.

330
00:23:04,817 --> 00:23:06,117
Anyway, uh, sorry.

331
00:23:06,185 --> 00:23:07,262
Well, here, come sit down.

332
00:23:07,286 --> 00:23:08,218
Thank you.

333
00:23:08,287 --> 00:23:10,065
Uh, now, where were we?

334
00:23:10,089 --> 00:23:11,321
Oh, um,

335
00:23:11,391 --> 00:23:15,392
do you know a Mitchell
Sands or a Jeffrey Barr?

336
00:23:15,461 --> 00:23:17,027
No.

337
00:23:19,131 --> 00:23:21,598
Would you mind taking a
look at this picture again?

338
00:23:29,975 --> 00:23:30,840
I don't know him.

339
00:23:30,909 --> 00:23:32,254
<i>Friend, I can look</i>

340
00:23:32,278 --> 00:23:35,078
at that picture all day, it's
not gonna change anything.

341
00:23:35,147 --> 00:23:37,248
I don't know this guy.

342
00:23:37,316 --> 00:23:39,350
Well, just one more question.

343
00:23:39,418 --> 00:23:41,218
How can you stand
working in this place?

344
00:23:42,321 --> 00:23:44,388
Do you sell
surveillance cameras?

345
00:23:44,457 --> 00:23:45,834
State-of-the-art
security systems.

346
00:23:45,858 --> 00:23:49,259
We provide for our commercial
and residential clients...

347
00:23:49,328 --> 00:23:51,829
Banks, jewelers,
uh, import-export.

348
00:23:51,897 --> 00:23:52,908
The list is endless.

349
00:23:52,932 --> 00:23:54,576
As well as the
private homeowner.

350
00:23:54,600 --> 00:23:57,401
Wait, you put cameras
in people's houses?

351
00:23:57,470 --> 00:23:59,936
Only if they don't
trust their relatives.

352
00:24:00,006 --> 00:24:01,271
Oh, I see.

353
00:24:01,340 --> 00:24:03,740
You tape the contents
of homes and businesses.

354
00:24:03,810 --> 00:24:05,609
In case they ever
are burglarized,

355
00:24:05,678 --> 00:24:07,956
they'll have a hard copy
record of their possessions

356
00:24:07,980 --> 00:24:09,280
for insurance purposes.

357
00:24:09,348 --> 00:24:10,280
Exactly.

358
00:24:10,349 --> 00:24:11,715
That's a great idea.

359
00:24:11,784 --> 00:24:13,884
Well, I'm sorry I can't help.

360
00:24:13,953 --> 00:24:15,151
Thanks, anyway.

361
00:24:17,022 --> 00:24:18,722
Just one more question.

362
00:24:18,791 --> 00:24:20,023
Sure.

363
00:24:20,092 --> 00:24:23,294
Where were you last Wednesday
evening, about 7:00 p.m.?

364
00:24:23,362 --> 00:24:26,129
Well, let's see here. Mon...

365
00:24:26,198 --> 00:24:28,098
Monday, Tuesday, uh, Wednesday.

366
00:24:28,167 --> 00:24:31,134
I was with Mr. And
Mrs. Lionel Dorfman,

367
00:24:31,203 --> 00:24:35,038
videotaping the contents
of their four-bedroom home.

368
00:24:35,107 --> 00:24:37,040
Okay.

369
00:25:10,208 --> 00:25:12,208
We got a major, major problem.

370
00:25:12,277 --> 00:25:13,688
No kidding. PROCTOR:
Should have known better

371
00:25:13,712 --> 00:25:15,590
than to put Rob Casey
in charge of getting rid

372
00:25:15,614 --> 00:25:16,992
of that stuff. How the hell were

373
00:25:17,016 --> 00:25:19,416
we supposed to know
he'd use it for blackmail?

374
00:25:19,485 --> 00:25:21,051
All right, what are we gonna do?

375
00:25:21,120 --> 00:25:22,964
There's only one
thing we can do.

376
00:25:22,988 --> 00:25:24,187
What?

377
00:25:24,256 --> 00:25:26,096
We find it and get rid of it.

378
00:25:26,158 --> 00:25:27,970
Now, he had to have
stashed the stuff somewhere.

379
00:25:27,994 --> 00:25:30,527
All right, but what
about this lawyer

380
00:25:30,596 --> 00:25:32,474
and these-these flunkies
he's got sniffing around?

381
00:25:32,498 --> 00:25:34,597
We know what we're looking for.

382
00:25:34,666 --> 00:25:36,166
They don't.

383
00:25:45,545 --> 00:25:46,788
You know Bob Brooks?

384
00:25:46,812 --> 00:25:48,712
I know who he is... a detective.

385
00:25:48,781 --> 00:25:50,926
Yeah. He gave me this key.

386
00:25:50,950 --> 00:25:53,095
Wanted to know
what I was looking for.

387
00:25:53,119 --> 00:25:54,284
Did you tell him?

388
00:25:54,353 --> 00:25:56,153
No.

389
00:25:56,222 --> 00:25:57,453
You don't know, do you?

390
00:25:59,325 --> 00:26:00,357
No.

391
00:26:06,332 --> 00:26:08,265
Oh.

392
00:26:08,334 --> 00:26:09,611
Oh.

393
00:26:09,635 --> 00:26:12,169
Well, whatever it was,
somebody beat us to it.

394
00:26:12,238 --> 00:26:13,703
Yeah.

395
00:26:16,442 --> 00:26:18,442
Right here.

396
00:26:41,933 --> 00:26:43,867
We got to get out of here!

397
00:26:43,936 --> 00:26:44,601
What?

398
00:26:44,670 --> 00:26:46,014
Gas! How's that?

399
00:26:46,038 --> 00:26:47,137
Come on!

400
00:26:48,608 --> 00:26:50,240
Don't go in there!

401
00:26:50,309 --> 00:26:51,687
What's going on? Gas!

402
00:26:51,711 --> 00:26:53,043
Wait!

403
00:27:03,923 --> 00:27:05,722
What did you say?

404
00:27:07,659 --> 00:27:09,559
I said gas.

405
00:27:09,629 --> 00:27:11,761
Gas.

406
00:27:22,608 --> 00:27:24,007
Ooh...

407
00:27:24,076 --> 00:27:26,020
Uh, Ben's hung up
giving a statement.

408
00:27:26,044 --> 00:27:27,589
He'll be back after a while.

409
00:27:27,613 --> 00:27:30,780
Ah. You mean the
house just blew right up?

410
00:27:30,849 --> 00:27:31,993
Yeah.

411
00:27:32,017 --> 00:27:33,584
It was a good show.

412
00:27:33,652 --> 00:27:35,586
Antiseptic?

413
00:27:36,722 --> 00:27:38,288
Thanks.

414
00:27:39,759 --> 00:27:41,291
Do you know Mitchell Sands?

415
00:27:41,360 --> 00:27:42,640
Car repair.

416
00:27:45,364 --> 00:27:47,530
Well, he's very
reluctant to talk.

417
00:27:47,599 --> 00:27:49,679
Uh, claims he was
stepping out on his wife

418
00:27:49,734 --> 00:27:50,854
the night of the murder.

419
00:27:50,903 --> 00:27:52,969
But the dame he was
supposed to be with

420
00:27:53,038 --> 00:27:54,470
was in Bermuda at the time.

421
00:27:54,539 --> 00:27:57,340
And all these corporate accounts
that he's supposed to have...

422
00:27:57,409 --> 00:27:59,449
None of the companies
have heard of him.

423
00:27:59,512 --> 00:28:00,856
So, how does he
stay in business?

424
00:28:00,880 --> 00:28:03,146
You tell me.

425
00:28:03,215 --> 00:28:05,615
I'll pick up my
son at the school,

426
00:28:05,685 --> 00:28:07,851
and I'll drop him
off at the sitter's.

427
00:28:07,920 --> 00:28:09,230
I'll stop by Mr. Sands'.

428
00:28:09,254 --> 00:28:10,399
I'll handle that.

429
00:28:10,423 --> 00:28:11,833
It'll be very simple for me.

430
00:28:11,857 --> 00:28:13,223
No simpler than for me.

431
00:28:13,292 --> 00:28:14,736
I have a car and everything.

432
00:28:14,760 --> 00:28:16,726
I didn't mean to
step on your toes.

433
00:28:16,796 --> 00:28:18,862
You didn't. I jumped
out of the way.

434
00:28:18,931 --> 00:28:20,697
May I make a suggestion?

435
00:28:20,766 --> 00:28:24,034
Why don't both of you go?

436
00:28:24,103 --> 00:28:27,604
Together, you know as a team?

437
00:28:30,743 --> 00:28:32,842
After you.

438
00:28:52,130 --> 00:28:53,764
Okay, let's go, short stuff.

439
00:28:53,833 --> 00:28:55,009
What's your name again?

440
00:28:55,033 --> 00:28:56,466
Tyler.

441
00:28:56,535 --> 00:28:58,145
Do you work for my mom?

442
00:28:58,169 --> 00:29:00,136
Not exactly.

443
00:29:03,142 --> 00:29:06,110
Mr. Hudson and I are
working together, honey.

444
00:29:06,178 --> 00:29:07,877
Sort of.

445
00:29:07,946 --> 00:29:09,980
Okay, here we are.

446
00:29:10,048 --> 00:29:12,882
Now, I won't be picking you
up until<i> after</i> dinner tonight.

447
00:29:12,951 --> 00:29:14,084
Mommy's working.

448
00:29:14,153 --> 00:29:15,497
Okay, Mommy. I love you.

449
00:29:15,521 --> 00:29:16,619
I love you, too.

450
00:29:16,689 --> 00:29:17,954
Big hug. Oh!

451
00:29:18,023 --> 00:29:20,690
Oh, and don't forget to
take your medicine, okay?

452
00:29:20,759 --> 00:29:22,359
Okay. Okay. Bye-bye.

453
00:29:22,428 --> 00:29:23,939
Bye.

454
00:29:23,963 --> 00:29:27,430
Mrs. Waverly, my mom's got
another guy working for her.

455
00:29:27,499 --> 00:29:29,165
Ooh. Come in.

456
00:29:36,908 --> 00:29:38,642
So, what do you think?

457
00:29:40,813 --> 00:29:42,345
About what?

458
00:29:42,414 --> 00:29:45,381
About the case.

459
00:29:45,450 --> 00:29:49,119
Well, the deceased needed
a lot of money in a hurry,

460
00:29:49,187 --> 00:29:51,922
and he went to some people
and tried to get it from them.

461
00:29:51,991 --> 00:29:54,335
Mitchell Sands, Nancy
Proctor, Jeffrey Barr.

462
00:29:54,359 --> 00:29:55,525
Right.

463
00:29:55,594 --> 00:29:57,105
And they all turned him down.

464
00:29:57,129 --> 00:29:59,596
And then he went out and
took those weird pictures

465
00:29:59,665 --> 00:30:01,832
to try to force the
money out of them.

466
00:30:01,900 --> 00:30:03,180
Blackmail.

467
00:30:03,235 --> 00:30:05,568
Ah, yes, a subject
with which I understand

468
00:30:05,638 --> 00:30:07,570
you are extremely familiar.

469
00:30:14,312 --> 00:30:15,924
Now, listen, Tyler, I'm
here, and I'm staying,

470
00:30:15,948 --> 00:30:17,158
so get used to it.

471
00:30:17,182 --> 00:30:19,461
I'm not proud of
the way I got this job,

472
00:30:19,485 --> 00:30:21,763
but I'd be a fool not to
take advantage of this...

473
00:30:21,787 --> 00:30:24,420
Oh, you have taken
advantage of it, all right.

474
00:30:24,490 --> 00:30:27,223
Damn right! This
is a tough business.

475
00:30:27,292 --> 00:30:29,726
You think I get to tell my
kid I go to work every day?

476
00:30:29,795 --> 00:30:31,206
Try once a week, if I'm lucky.

477
00:30:31,230 --> 00:30:32,741
That's right. Bring up the kid.

478
00:30:32,765 --> 00:30:33,697
What's that?

479
00:30:33,765 --> 00:30:35,465
Nothing. Just turn around.

480
00:30:35,534 --> 00:30:37,612
I thought we were
gonna go see Sands.

481
00:30:37,636 --> 00:30:39,302
Turn around. Why?

482
00:30:39,371 --> 00:30:41,604
I have to make a stop... alone.

483
00:30:41,673 --> 00:30:43,040
Some personal business.

484
00:30:43,108 --> 00:30:45,441
You stay in the car.

485
00:30:45,511 --> 00:30:47,210
You understand?

486
00:30:47,279 --> 00:30:48,489
No problem.

487
00:30:48,513 --> 00:30:49,645
Hmm.

488
00:31:14,539 --> 00:31:17,407
Ben, I work alone.

489
00:31:19,511 --> 00:31:22,345
Oh. Linda giving you trouble?

490
00:31:22,414 --> 00:31:25,248
Not trouble, exactly.

491
00:31:25,317 --> 00:31:27,250
Well, what is it, exactly?

492
00:31:27,319 --> 00:31:31,855
Well, it just... Just what?

493
00:31:31,924 --> 00:31:35,926
It just galls me the
way she got this job.

494
00:31:35,995 --> 00:31:37,961
Oh.

495
00:31:38,030 --> 00:31:41,365
Yeah, it galled me
a little at first, too,

496
00:31:41,433 --> 00:31:43,333
but you got to hand it to her.

497
00:31:43,402 --> 00:31:45,768
She-she saw what she
wanted, and she went for it.

498
00:31:45,837 --> 00:31:48,138
Either one of us would
have done the same thing.

499
00:31:48,207 --> 00:31:50,073
Well, I suppose.

500
00:31:50,141 --> 00:31:52,208
Well, what's the trouble?

501
00:31:52,278 --> 00:31:54,611
Well, she's got a kid.

502
00:31:54,680 --> 00:31:55,690
I know it.

503
00:31:55,714 --> 00:31:57,581
And he thinks I work for her.

504
00:31:59,084 --> 00:32:03,419
If anything happens to
her, that kid's an orphan.

505
00:32:03,488 --> 00:32:05,728
Now I am trying to conduct
an investigation here,

506
00:32:05,757 --> 00:32:07,836
and I got to look after
some kid's mother?

507
00:32:07,860 --> 00:32:12,629
Well, nobody was looking
after Linda before us.

508
00:32:12,698 --> 00:32:14,698
I'm sure she can
take care of herself.

509
00:32:17,602 --> 00:32:20,269
I work alone.

510
00:32:20,339 --> 00:32:24,274
Tyler, I know we'd all
like things to be the way

511
00:32:24,343 --> 00:32:28,311
they've always been, but
sometimes they're just not.

512
00:32:28,380 --> 00:32:30,424
Now, I made a
deal with this girl

513
00:32:30,448 --> 00:32:32,994
for the information she had.

514
00:32:33,018 --> 00:32:36,519
And the deal is
a job on this case.

515
00:32:36,588 --> 00:32:39,256
I don't know what
else to tell you.

516
00:32:54,139 --> 00:32:56,172
How dare you walk in here

517
00:32:56,241 --> 00:32:57,907
and make an
accusation like that.

518
00:32:57,976 --> 00:32:59,520
I'm not accusing
you of anything.

519
00:32:59,544 --> 00:33:01,523
I'm just stating the
facts. Get out of here.

520
00:33:01,547 --> 00:33:04,847
Your alibi doesn't wash, and
your company here's a fraud.

521
00:33:04,917 --> 00:33:06,883
Get out of here.

522
00:33:06,952 --> 00:33:08,985
You can explain
here or in court.

523
00:33:09,054 --> 00:33:10,487
I said get the hell out of here!

524
00:33:11,290 --> 00:33:12,089
Now!

525
00:33:12,157 --> 00:33:14,858
You got trouble, fella.

526
00:34:27,565 --> 00:34:29,065
Sands.

527
00:35:00,199 --> 00:35:02,465
♪ ♪

528
00:35:18,417 --> 00:35:19,417
Whoa!

529
00:35:22,754 --> 00:35:24,599
Can you make
that out right there?

530
00:35:24,623 --> 00:35:26,601
Well, it looks like
some kind of a label,

531
00:35:26,625 --> 00:35:28,836
but it's not, it's
too small to read.

532
00:35:28,860 --> 00:35:31,260
Too small. I'd have
to blow it up bigger.

533
00:35:33,431 --> 00:35:35,944
These pictures of these
guns and whatever this is,

534
00:35:35,968 --> 00:35:38,802
those three people
Rob Casey knew

535
00:35:38,870 --> 00:35:40,815
had to be real
interested in this stuff.

536
00:35:40,839 --> 00:35:44,285
I bet whoever blew up his
house is looking for this box.

537
00:35:46,544 --> 00:35:49,145
Which one of you
is Ben Matlocks?

538
00:35:49,214 --> 00:35:52,248
Uh, I'm Ben Matlock.

539
00:35:54,152 --> 00:35:56,064
Mr. Matlocks and I
need to talk in private.

540
00:35:56,088 --> 00:35:58,799
Uh, hey, you can't come in
here and just tell people that...

541
00:35:58,823 --> 00:36:00,189
Say good-bye, Mr. Matlocks.

542
00:36:00,259 --> 00:36:02,819
Michael, I'll see you later.

543
00:36:07,399 --> 00:36:11,368
My name is Matlock...
Ck-ck-ck-ck-ck!

544
00:36:11,436 --> 00:36:14,771
My employer wants to
see you, Mr. Matlocks.

545
00:36:46,171 --> 00:36:50,039
Mr. Matlock, Dom
Vincent. Pleased to meet ya.

546
00:36:51,610 --> 00:36:53,943
Dom Vincent? Not the, uh...?

547
00:36:54,012 --> 00:36:56,179
Yes.

548
00:36:56,248 --> 00:36:58,848
I'm surprised we
haven't met before.

549
00:36:58,917 --> 00:36:59,928
I'm not.

550
00:36:59,952 --> 00:37:02,485
You defend murderers.

551
00:37:02,554 --> 00:37:04,787
Me, I'm just a businessman.

552
00:37:04,856 --> 00:37:05,922
Oh.

553
00:37:05,991 --> 00:37:07,123
You play?

554
00:37:07,192 --> 00:37:10,660
Uh, no, I never
got the hang of it.

555
00:37:10,729 --> 00:37:14,998
How about a little gentleman's
wager, say, $50 that I can

556
00:37:15,067 --> 00:37:15,898
birdie this hole?

557
00:37:15,968 --> 00:37:17,033
What do you say?

558
00:37:17,102 --> 00:37:18,768
Oh, I don't...

559
00:37:18,837 --> 00:37:21,370
I don't believe I got $50 on me.

560
00:37:21,440 --> 00:37:22,480
Don't worry about it.

561
00:37:22,507 --> 00:37:23,985
I'll lend it to you.

562
00:37:24,009 --> 00:37:25,642
Excuse me.

563
00:37:42,360 --> 00:37:44,494
I...

564
00:37:44,563 --> 00:37:46,773
believe it went
in that-that little...

565
00:37:46,797 --> 00:37:48,642
No... bunch of trees
right there, just...

566
00:37:48,666 --> 00:37:51,033
I think I kinda caught
the edge of the fairway

567
00:37:51,102 --> 00:37:53,069
right out there.

568
00:37:53,137 --> 00:37:55,705
Check it out.

569
00:37:55,774 --> 00:37:58,841
Mr. Matlock and I are
gonna walk. Come on.

570
00:38:16,160 --> 00:38:17,705
My people

571
00:38:17,729 --> 00:38:21,497
are detaining someone we caught
trespassing on my property yesterday.

572
00:38:21,566 --> 00:38:24,300
He says his name
is Tyler Hudson.

573
00:38:24,369 --> 00:38:27,169
Yeah, he works for me.

574
00:38:27,239 --> 00:38:29,884
I don't know what's he's
doing... doing on your property,

575
00:38:29,908 --> 00:38:32,742
but if somebody found him there,

576
00:38:32,811 --> 00:38:34,589
I'm sure he had good reason.

577
00:38:34,613 --> 00:38:37,113
He also states he was
following someone you think

578
00:38:37,181 --> 00:38:38,748
was involved in a murder.

579
00:38:38,817 --> 00:38:44,320
Oh... probably Mitchell
Sands and Jeffrey Barr.

580
00:38:44,389 --> 00:38:48,758
Now what makes you think that
Mitchell was involved in a murder?

581
00:38:48,827 --> 00:38:50,326
Well, I don't know.

582
00:38:50,395 --> 00:38:52,573
For one thing, he
lied about his alibi.

583
00:38:52,597 --> 00:38:53,841
Hey, Dom, you were right.

584
00:38:53,865 --> 00:38:56,632
It's right here. Great shot.

585
00:38:59,704 --> 00:39:02,105
Excuse me. Eight iron.

586
00:39:21,559 --> 00:39:23,337
It went in that pond over there.

587
00:39:23,361 --> 00:39:26,295
Think so? I lost it in the sun.

588
00:39:26,364 --> 00:39:28,798
Yeah... Think it went that way.

589
00:39:28,867 --> 00:39:30,433
Check it out.

590
00:39:32,203 --> 00:39:34,370
Mr. Matlock...

591
00:39:34,439 --> 00:39:38,340
there's something that you
should know about Mitchell Sands.

592
00:39:38,410 --> 00:39:41,177
Mitch and I do
business together.

593
00:39:41,246 --> 00:39:43,779
He fix your cars?

594
00:39:43,848 --> 00:39:45,881
Occasionally.

595
00:39:45,951 --> 00:39:47,550
I don't understand.

596
00:39:47,618 --> 00:39:51,587
How does he do it
when none of his trucks

597
00:39:51,656 --> 00:39:55,024
ever, ever leave his garage?

598
00:39:56,527 --> 00:39:58,027
Diversification.

599
00:39:58,096 --> 00:40:02,966
The major part of Mitch's
cash flow is derived

600
00:40:03,034 --> 00:40:07,036
from sources outside of
his auto repair business.

601
00:40:08,573 --> 00:40:10,017
That doesn't make any sense.

602
00:40:10,041 --> 00:40:11,174
No?

603
00:40:11,242 --> 00:40:12,387
Hey, Dom?

604
00:40:12,411 --> 00:40:15,211
Hell of a shot!
You're hot today, huh?

605
00:40:15,280 --> 00:40:18,214
Give me my putter.

606
00:40:22,854 --> 00:40:24,421
All right.

607
00:40:34,866 --> 00:40:37,300
Uh, Mitchell Sands' alibi?

608
00:40:38,369 --> 00:40:39,669
I'm putting.

609
00:40:45,410 --> 00:40:46,410
Yeah!

610
00:40:46,445 --> 00:40:47,377
All right.

611
00:40:47,445 --> 00:40:49,345
Mitch has an alibi.

612
00:40:49,414 --> 00:40:51,647
I prefer not to go into details,

613
00:40:51,716 --> 00:40:55,651
but you have my word
on it as a gentleman.

614
00:40:59,490 --> 00:41:00,723
Thank you, Mr. Matlock.

615
00:41:17,241 --> 00:41:19,275
Hi.

616
00:41:19,343 --> 00:41:21,544
Arsonist report's in
on Rob Casey's house.

617
00:41:21,613 --> 00:41:23,112
They say it was an accident.

618
00:41:23,181 --> 00:41:25,147
Yeah or
top-of-the-line arsonist.

619
00:41:25,216 --> 00:41:30,286
Okay, one portable safe made
by the Century Safe Company

620
00:41:30,354 --> 00:41:32,722
and identical to the
one Rob Casey dug up.

621
00:41:32,791 --> 00:41:33,868
Hmm.

622
00:41:33,892 --> 00:41:35,636
You know, they sell
these things to everybody:

623
00:41:35,660 --> 00:41:39,629
banks, motels, hotels,
pawnshops, museums.

624
00:41:39,698 --> 00:41:42,064
We have to find that one.

625
00:41:42,133 --> 00:41:44,767
Maybe somewhere
in Linda's notes.

626
00:41:46,237 --> 00:41:49,772
You know, if someone
else is looking for that safe,

627
00:41:49,840 --> 00:41:51,760
they may try to
get Linda's notes.

628
00:42:01,652 --> 00:42:02,818
Busy.

629
00:42:35,053 --> 00:42:37,820
I'm sorry. Your husband,
Rob Casey, does have

630
00:42:37,889 --> 00:42:40,823
a P.O. box here, but I'm
afraid I can't open it for you.

631
00:42:40,892 --> 00:42:41,824
Why not?

632
00:42:41,893 --> 00:42:42,925
Federal law.

633
00:42:42,994 --> 00:42:45,094
Your name's not
on the application.

634
00:42:45,163 --> 00:42:46,362
It should be.

635
00:42:46,430 --> 00:42:47,830
Can I see that?

636
00:42:52,270 --> 00:42:53,970
Thanks, anyway.

637
00:42:54,038 --> 00:42:55,638
Sorry.

638
00:42:58,877 --> 00:43:00,187
Excuse me. Excuse me.

639
00:43:03,347 --> 00:43:06,482
Hi. On the 17th of this month,

640
00:43:06,551 --> 00:43:08,963
a fellow by the name of
Rob Casey came in here.

641
00:43:08,987 --> 00:43:11,498
Now, does he have a post
office box or something here?

642
00:43:11,522 --> 00:43:12,889
As a matter of fact, he does.

643
00:43:12,958 --> 00:43:14,357
What's the number?

644
00:43:14,426 --> 00:43:17,159
I'm sorry. I can't give
out that information,

645
00:43:17,228 --> 00:43:18,728
but Mrs. Casey's just leaving.

646
00:43:18,797 --> 00:43:21,142
If you hurry up and catch her,
she might be able to help you.

647
00:43:21,166 --> 00:43:23,332
Mrs. Casey?!

648
00:43:46,690 --> 00:43:48,123
Shoot.

649
00:43:48,193 --> 00:43:51,033
<i>After he re-entered
the coin shop,</i>

650
00:43:51,096 --> 00:43:53,229
what did the defendant do?

651
00:43:53,298 --> 00:43:57,133
He sort of pushed Mr. Casey.

652
00:43:57,202 --> 00:43:58,212
He pushed him?

653
00:43:58,236 --> 00:43:59,736
Yes.

654
00:43:59,804 --> 00:44:00,736
Hard?

655
00:44:00,805 --> 00:44:02,104
Yes.

656
00:44:02,173 --> 00:44:05,574
Would you say that the,
uh, defendant was angry?

657
00:44:05,644 --> 00:44:08,611
He was very angry.

658
00:44:08,679 --> 00:44:10,246
Then what did he do?

659
00:44:10,315 --> 00:44:11,947
He tried to strangle him.

660
00:44:12,016 --> 00:44:15,050
My friend down at the DMV
tells me that the car that I saw

661
00:44:15,120 --> 00:44:17,431
at the post office
belongs to Nancy Proctor.

662
00:44:17,455 --> 00:44:19,066
He was so angry, he tried to...

663
00:44:19,090 --> 00:44:21,668
So I guess our friends have
gotten ahold of Linda's notebook.

664
00:44:21,692 --> 00:44:23,036
I had to pull Mr. Koskoff off.

665
00:44:23,060 --> 00:44:24,905
Have you found her yet? No.

666
00:44:24,929 --> 00:44:27,708
Thank you, Mr. Davis. That's all.
You want me to check her office?

667
00:44:27,732 --> 00:44:29,632
No, the prosecution
subpoenaed her.

668
00:44:29,700 --> 00:44:31,267
She should be here any minute.

669
00:44:31,336 --> 00:44:32,268
Okay.

670
00:44:32,337 --> 00:44:33,948
Mr. Matlock, do
you wish to cross?

671
00:44:33,972 --> 00:44:35,571
No questions, Your Honor.

672
00:44:35,639 --> 00:44:37,284
The witness may step down.

673
00:44:37,308 --> 00:44:39,541
Call the next witness, please.

674
00:44:39,611 --> 00:44:42,945
I call Ms., uh, Linda
Hansfield to the stand.

675
00:44:53,057 --> 00:44:55,569
What does he want with her?

676
00:44:55,593 --> 00:44:56,992
He's gonna use her

677
00:44:57,061 --> 00:45:01,029
to establish the
exact time of death.

678
00:45:01,098 --> 00:45:03,699
You don't have an alibi.

679
00:45:03,768 --> 00:45:07,136
About how far away from
Mr. Casey's house were you parked?

680
00:45:07,204 --> 00:45:09,472
About 30 yards or so.

681
00:45:09,541 --> 00:45:12,541
So Mr. Casey was inside
and you were outside.

682
00:45:12,610 --> 00:45:13,610
What happened?

683
00:45:15,313 --> 00:45:17,679
At exactly 6:12, I
heard two shots fired

684
00:45:17,748 --> 00:45:19,915
inside Mr. Casey's house.

685
00:45:19,984 --> 00:45:21,550
I investigated immediately.

686
00:45:21,619 --> 00:45:24,487
The front door was locked,
so I ran around to the back door

687
00:45:24,555 --> 00:45:25,821
which was wide open.

688
00:45:25,890 --> 00:45:27,322
And what did you do?

689
00:45:27,392 --> 00:45:31,560
I entered and saw Mr. Casey
on the living room floor.

690
00:45:31,628 --> 00:45:32,728
He was dead.

691
00:45:32,797 --> 00:45:34,697
Then what did you do?

692
00:45:34,766 --> 00:45:37,633
Then I thought I
heard a car starting up

693
00:45:37,702 --> 00:45:40,069
in the alley out back,
so I ran around to look.

694
00:45:40,138 --> 00:45:42,070
And what did you see?

695
00:45:45,075 --> 00:45:48,177
I saw the defendant,
Michael Koskoff, driving away.

696
00:45:48,246 --> 00:45:50,612
You're certain that it
was Michael Koskoff?

697
00:45:52,650 --> 00:45:53,650
I'm positive.

698
00:45:53,718 --> 00:45:54,995
No further questions,
Your Honor.

699
00:45:55,019 --> 00:45:56,952
Do you wish to
cross, Mr. Matlock?

700
00:45:57,021 --> 00:45:59,121
You're damn right, I do.

701
00:45:59,190 --> 00:46:00,556
Mr. Matlock!

702
00:46:00,625 --> 00:46:01,390
What?!

703
00:46:01,459 --> 00:46:02,891
Watch your language.

704
00:46:02,961 --> 00:46:05,528
I'm sorry, Your Honor.
Yes, I wish to cross.

705
00:46:22,680 --> 00:46:25,080
What's your name, again?

706
00:46:26,184 --> 00:46:27,783
Linda Hansfield.

707
00:46:27,852 --> 00:46:30,119
The same Linda Hansfield

708
00:46:30,188 --> 00:46:33,823
who gave a long, detailed
statement to the police

709
00:46:33,891 --> 00:46:38,727
the night she found Rob Casey
murdered in his living room?

710
00:46:38,797 --> 00:46:40,095
Yes.

711
00:46:40,164 --> 00:46:41,530
And in that statement

712
00:46:41,599 --> 00:46:45,301
you said nothing about hearing
a car or going back outside

713
00:46:45,369 --> 00:46:47,114
or seeing the
defendant drive away.

714
00:46:47,138 --> 00:46:48,737
Why is that, Ms. Hansfield?

715
00:46:50,374 --> 00:46:52,041
Did you think it
wasn't important?

716
00:46:52,109 --> 00:46:53,575
Did you forget?

717
00:46:53,645 --> 00:46:55,489
Did it just suddenly
come to you?

718
00:46:55,513 --> 00:46:57,491
Objection, Your Honor.
Somebody got to you. Who was it?

719
00:46:57,515 --> 00:46:58,959
Mr. Matlock is
badgering the witness.

720
00:46:58,983 --> 00:47:00,594
Who got to you, Linda?!
Objection, Your Honor!

721
00:47:00,618 --> 00:47:03,185
I know what I saw!

722
00:47:04,555 --> 00:47:06,622
I know what I saw.

9999
00:00:0,500 --> 00:00:2,00
